# PROJECT_CONTEXT → Notion BYOFA

`PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` is the **only repo source of truth** for shipped vs planned. [BYOFA Features](https://www.notion.so/BYOFA-Features-35fa694147bf8093be2fc57673cee41a) is the stakeholder-facing copy: inline **Feature Roadmap Table** (`collection://363a6941-47bf-81d1-9580-000baf6b7dd3`).

When you **materially edit** `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` (feature inventory rows added/removed, status changes, or “Last reviewed”), or the user asks to **sync BYOFA**, **sync Notion from PROJECT_CONTEXT**, or **update the roadmap table**, reconcile Notion using the **Notion MCP** (`user-notion`).

There is **no** `docs/feature_roadmap.md` — do not recreate it unless the user asks.

## Step 1 — Read inventory

Parse **[Feature inventory (shipped vs planned)]** and **Roadmap modules (Planning cards only)**. Use **Routes** / **Database** only for extra context when writing **What it does** / **Next step**.

Expand **Roadmap modules** into one Notion row each when listed there and not already a dedicated inventory row: Insurance tracking, Scenario simulator, Dependents planning, Estate checklist, Wealth reports (quarterly reports), Documents vault, Risk profiling, Account syncing, Retirement planning studio (Partial), AI insights (Planned — also inventory Home row).

Split broad inventory lines into product rows where Notion already uses separate titles (e.g. Home metrics → Client home dashboard, Net worth summary, Monthly spending view; proposals → Advisor proposal flow + Proposal review page).

## Step 2 — Build Notion row payloads

For each product row, set:

| Notion property | Source |
|-----------------|--------|
| **Feature** (title) | Product name from mapping table below |
| **Status** | See status mapping |
| **What it does** | One plain-language sentence from inventory **Notes** (no file paths, no backticks) |
| **Area** / **User Type** | From mapping defaults |
| **Priority** | Default from mapping; if row exists in Notion, **keep** current Priority unless status flipped to Partial/Planned on a formerly Done item → bump toward High |
| **Next step** | Short action from inventory gap; if row exists in Notion and inventory unchanged, **keep** existing Next step |

| `PROJECT_CONTEXT` status | Notion **Status** |
|--------------------------|-------------------|
| **Shipped** | Done |
| **Partial** | Partial |
| **Planned** | Planned |
| **Not in repo** | Missing |

**User Type** for scope rows: `Admin` or `Needs confirmation` as in mapping. Others: Client, Advisor, or Both.

